## codex-zig-transpiler: the same gap, keyboard work done

`guest.wrap` wrote mode line, bundle and terminator. `source/resolve_unit.ps1`
makes compile.ps1's two calls and writes the result INTO the bundled file, so
stage 7 (native) still reads what stage 4 (the seed) read. `build.py`'s
`bundle()` runs it after each bundler.

Resolving the transpiler subject raised compile.ps1's own WARNING: five
forewords (Maybe, Wrap64, Fat16, ImportGate, FactDisk) that
`bundle_codexzig.ps1` listed under Parsmi. plug-build-lib asks about presence
FIRST, so it took `Parsmi--Maybe` as Maybe. quire-map's `Resolve-CiteOrder`
consults presence only when the chapter's FILE is missing; otherwise it needs a
`Foreword--Maybe` header. compile.ps1 would therefore have bundled each twice.
The bundler no longer lists them, and plug-build-lib brings them as
`Foreword--<name>`, as it does CCE.

Guest-free at U60, each of the five appears once as `Foreword--<name>`, the
resolver adds nothing, and the bundle holds 6,586 definitions, the same
multiset as before with none defined twice.

**The two resolvers disagree about presence, and neither rule is new.**
`Resolve-CiteOrder` checks presence only when the chapter's file is missing, a
rule from Update 35 (`faf1c639`). The implicit ListUtils/Tuple walk arrived in
Update 36 (`b1c50258`). plug-build-lib's "Presence is asked FIRST" is OUR PR 69
(landed `a061c173`, 2026-08-19), which fixed exactly this ordering in
`Resolve-PlugForewords` and left `Resolve-CiteOrder` unchanged. U59 only put
the first `for` into a chapter we bundle. Tracked, and not a finding:
cobblestone-qemu `FINDINGS.md` section 3.

`generated/` was cleaned first (Steve): the dirty 2026-09-10 artifacts were
restored to HEAD and the ignored cache deleted.

